# L §4.2 Date arithmetic defines date ± duration and date ± int; the difference of two dates is days_between(a, b).
# L §8.4: an operation with no meaning for the types it is given is refused at load (LOAD-UNIT).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input a: date
input b: date
def c: int = b - a at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  a = 2026-01-01
  b = 2026-03-01

ask q: c law 2026-06-30
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT ...
